    {
      "id": "all",
      "type": "collection.rasterize_contours",
      "name": "Preserve all topology",
      "description": "Expected foreground area: 15,168 pixels.",
      "documentation": "<p>Rasterize each related contour subtree as a group, then union independent roots. This preserves holes and islands without XOR cancellation between independent parts. A selected hole is treated as a new foreground root. Missing hierarchy links are reported; no absent holes are invented.</p><p><a href=\"https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/imgproc_draw.html\">OpenCV drawing reference</a>. Subpixel fills use fillPoly; whole-pixel fills use drawContours. Outlines use polylines. Masks are binary, not alpha coverage.</p>",
      "parameters": {
        "selection": "all",
        "items": [],
        "topology": "hierarchy",
        "include_descendants": true,
        "maximum_depth": -1,
        "mode": "filled",
        "thickness": 1,
        "line_type": "8_connected",
        "subpixel_bits": 0,
        "offset": [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        "invert": false,
        "alignment": "same_frame",
        "check_pixels": true,
        "minimum_pixels": 15168,
        "maximum_pixels": 15168
      },
      "position": [
        250.0,
        0.0
